Title: Exclude the arena skill from contestant pins
Created: 2026-10-29
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-10-29T11:38Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Arena run 2026-10-29 (arena repo, docs/smoke-2026-10-29/README.md and
memory/journal/2026/2026-10-29-arena-run-smoke-and-free-panel.md): in the smoke
leg f1m (excursion scan HARNESS 1) the contestant read its own pinned `arena`
skill, a possible leak of the bench's method to the contestant.

Mechanism (read-only search, harness side): the contestant's skill set is the
Pi skills directories. `~/.pi/agent/skills/arena` is a symlink to the arena
repo's `skills/arena`, left over from the per-skill Pi links that `idh install`
created before PR 1690 (2026-10-27) moved Pi to the standard root. Pi now reads
`~/.agents/skills`, projected by `adapters/projections.json` (entry
`~/.agents/skills` -> `$IDH_ROOT/skills`, runtimes codex and pi, children).
The arena's `harness_pin.py` copies `skills/` from the live Pi agent dir into
the sealed snapshot, so whatever is linked at pin time is what the contestant sees.
The harness has no `skills/arena`: the link is not in the manifest, so
`idh install` neither declares nor retires it.

Proposal (to choose in Plan): the arena-owned skill set that must not reach a
contestant is declared as a harness-visible exclusion (e.g. a bench-only skill
marker or a pin-time deny list honoured by `idh`/the Pi projection), rather
than relying on hand-removal of a stray link. The pin copy itself lives in the
arena repo and is not edited from here.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The mechanism that puts `arena` in a pinned skill set is named in the fix and documented.
- [ ] A pin built after the fix contains no `arena` skill (checked on a fresh pin).
- [ ] `make check` passes.
